{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nClosing `fb5f-54fd-96cc-4105` through MCP `transition_ticket` was refused with\n\"has unchecked Acceptance Criteria items\", quoting the pre-edit description, while\nMCP `show_ticket` already returned the edited description (0 `- [ ]`, `updated_at`\nequal to the EDIT event). The boxes were ticked from a different clone (a local\nworktree) and pushed. The same close then succeeded through the local CLI. An\noperator following the refusal has nothing left to do except `--force`.\n\n## Findings (code path, evidence in comments)\n\n- `transition_ticket` is in-process: the MCP spec maps it to the library\n  `rebar.transition` -> `transition_compute` -> `transition_close.close_ticket`.\n  It reads the same `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` clone as the read tools. Hypothesis 1 (a\n  subprocess on a second clone) is refuted.\n- The deployed server does not run the pinned view: 0 of the 400 most recent\n  COMPLETION_VERDICT events carry `completion_read_basis`, and the MCP verdicts on\n  `fb5f` record `material_basis: unpinned_completion_inputs`. So hypothesis 2 is\n  refuted as stated; with the view off, `close_precheck` passes no state and\n  `txn.ensure_ac_boxes_checked` reduces the ticket from the server clone's files.\n- The defect: nothing on the close path fetches. `close_ticket` and\n  `_completion_precheck` read ticket type, plan-review material, AC boxes and the\n  landing scan from whatever the clone holds. Only read tools call\n  `reads.ensure_fresh`, throttled to one fetch per 60 s by a shared marker, so a\n  close sees another clone's edit only if some read happened to reconverge first.\n- `check_ac` is not evidence of ticked boxes: `check_ac_compute` counts criteria\n  lines (`criteria_count >= 1` passes) and never inspects `[x]`/`[ ]`.\n- Prior intent: ticket `glandulous-minor-aurochs` decided \"gate material reads force\n  one fetch; other reads keep the 60 s throttle\" (`ensure_fresh(force=True)`,\n  best-effort, honors `sync.pull=off`). Ticket `thin-broadish-basenji` set the close\n  path to read the tracker \"current-at-close\". This applies both to the close.\n\nUnverified: why one incident retry window lasted minutes rather than 60 s; the\nserver's logs were not inspected. The fix does not depend on it.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd `_refresh_close_material(tracker, force_close)` in\n`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py` and call it at the top of the close\nbranch of `close_ticket` (target `closed`, source not `idea`), before the first\n`reduce_ticket`. Unforced closes run `reads.ensure_fresh(tracker, force=True)`\nonce: one best-effort fetch + reconverge that skips only the 60 s age check, keeps\nthe `sync.pull=off`, `--no-pull` and local-read-context opt-outs, writes the marker\nand swallows every failure (an unreachable origin closes on local state exactly as\ntoday). Forced closes skip it: they bypass every gate that reads this material.\nIt runs outside the write lock, as the existing close checks do, so no fetch runs\nunder the lock. Every later read in the close (type, plan-review recheck, AC\nboxes, attested items, landing scan, the pinned view's HEAD capture when that\nexperiment is on) then sees the synced clone. No new config, env var or flag.\n\nDocument in `docs/concurrency.md` (read-freshness policy) that gate material\nreads, now including an unforced close, force one fetch past the throttle.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py`: the helper and its single call.\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_fresh_ac_material.py`: new tests.\n- `docs/concurrency.md`: one paragraph in the read-freshness policy.\n\nOut of scope: claim-time currency (`fabulous-avian-hoverfly`), `check_ac`\nsemantics, enabling the pinned view.\n\n## Testing\n\nTwo clones of one bare `tickets` origin: clone A (editor) and clone B (the\n\"server\", `require_completion_verification_for_close = true`). The throttle marker\nfor B is stamped fresh, as on a busy server. `rebar.llm.verify_completion` is\nstubbed, so no LLM runs. Close goes through `rebar.transition(repo_root=B)`, the\nentry point MCP `transition_ticket` calls.\n\n1. Satisfied: A ticks every box and pushes; B closes. Before the fix B refuses\n   with the stale unchecked items (reproduced); after, it closes.\n2. Unsatisfied: B already holds a ticked description; A unticks one box and pushes;\n   B's close is refused naming that item, matching a fresh `show_ticket`. Before\n   the fix B closes on the stale ticks.\n3. Opt-out: with `REBAR_SYNC_PULL=off`, the close makes no fetch (fetch spy count\n   0) and judges local state.\n4. Unreachable origin: remote URL points nowhere; the close does not raise from\n   the fetch and judges local state (refused on stale items).\n5. Forced close: no fetch attempted.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The source `transition_ticket`'s AC precheck reads is identified, and\n      which of the 2 hypotheses holds is stated with evidence from the code\n      path, not inference from the error string.\n- [ ] A regression test fails before the fix and passes after: a close through\n      `rebar.transition` (the entry point MCP `transition_ticket` uses), on a clone\n      whose throttle marker is fresh, observes a description edit pushed from\n      another clone.\n- [ ] For the same ticket at the same moment, the close precheck and a fresh\n      `show_ticket` agree on the AC boxes, for both a satisfied and an\n      unsatisfied ticket (tests 1 and 2).\n- [ ] The forced fetch honors `sync.pull=off`, survives an unreachable origin,\n      and is skipped on a forced close (tests 3-5).\n- [ ] Targeted tests, `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass locally, and the\n      change has `Verified +1` in Gerrit (the CI run of the `make test` selection)."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793539926680344001,"uuid":"1417f9d3-d08c-4183-b907-5ee61a164d2b"}